{
  "method": "perf stat hardware counters, controlled by named FIFO acknowledgements immediately around the measured call loop; imports, fixture construction, correctness checks, and 10 warmups excluded",
  "commands": {
    "prefix": "PYTHONPATH=python:benchmarks perf stat -D -1 --control=fifo:/tmp/dcborperf.ctl,/tmp/dcborperf.ack -o /tmp/{tag}_roi.txt -e cycles:u,instructions:u,branches:u,branch-misses:u,cache-references:u,cache-misses:u -- .venv/bin/python benchmarks/v02_profile/profile_native.py --perf-control-prefix /tmp/dcborperf --fixture {fixture} --operation {operation} --rounds {rounds} --warmup 10",
    "helper_sha256": "535b9f552d596ba8aa9e6d283aa51bdbe2492b26b55d996fe58985c873cf0718",
    "extension_sha256": "ca06f077c3ca1f2a72270b06d5799bc851a7612dec4728e6407839fe95aa1a94"
  },
  "environment": {
    "cpu": "AMD Ryzen 7 7435HS",
    "kernel": "Linux 7.2.4-200.fc44.x86_64",
    "cpu_governor": "powersave",
    "perf_event_paranoid": 2,
    "perf_version": "perf 7.2.4"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "These are hardware counter totals from a FIFO-controlled ROI around the codec-call loop, normalized by loop call count.",
    "The ROI includes Python loop/lambda dispatch, result reference replacement/release, PyO3 and extension work, plus small enable-ack/disable-command boundary overhead; it is not Rust-only attribution.",
    "They are not elapsed time; no branch-predictor, cache, or pipeline cause is inferred from counts alone.",
    "Profiler counters were not collected in the same run as committed normal timing medians.",
    "The helper consumed and validated each FIFO ack but retained no ack transcript; no raw ack lines are available.",
    "perf_stat_raw.txt preserves the original printed fields with trailing column-padding spaces trimmed."
  ],
